  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppRC 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After several months of post-approval use, follow-up surveys show that
    some patients are experiencing ongoing fatigue that affects daily activities.
    You summarize this pattern in a report.


    <b>What is the research coordinator
    expected to do next?</b>'
  explanation: Research coordinators help communicate findings by organizing and
    sharing post-approval information with the right teams. Sharing these summaries
    helps clinicians, researchers, and public health partners recognize patterns
    over time and decide whether further review, communication, or follow-up is needed.
    This ensures patient experiences continue to inform care and safety decisions
    even after a treatment is approved.
  correctAnswer: 'Share the reported pattern with the research team '
  incorrectAnswer1: Decide whether the treatment is effective based on the reported
    pattern
  incorrectAnswer2: Make a list of recommended changes to patient care
  incorrectAnswer3: Decide whether additional safety studies are required
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
